  "id": "Compound::DB00338 - Gene::9429",
  "verbalization": "Omeprazole and Abcg2 are linked through a shared mechanism involving the binding of certain compounds to Abcg2. The evidence suggests that Omeprazole, a proton pump inhibitor, causes Anterior Ischemic Optic Neuropathy, which is subsequently caused by Pantoprazole, a similar class of drug. Pantoprazole binds to Abcg2, indicating a potential role for this transporter in the pathophysiology of the condition. Similarly, Omeprazole is associated with Vitamin B12 Deficiency, which is caused by Folic Acid, and Folic Acid binds to Abcg2. This suggests that Abcg2 may be involved in the transport or regulation of these compounds, possibly through a common pathway involving organic heterobicyclic compounds. The integration of these findings implies that Abcg2 may play a role in the metabolic or transport processes affected by these drugs, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
